scallassig@mailexpire.com (Harald Korneliussen) writes:
> psmithnews@spod-central.org (Dylan O'Donnell) wrote in message 
> [...] 
> > You can always specify 'name:player' in your .nethackrc (or, indeed,
> > '-u player' from the command line), which will force the game to ask
> > you for a character name at start-up.
> 
> That (name:player) is exactly the thing I had been looking for. Is
> that in the guidebook? (I think I tried name:ask once)

No, it's not; also, it'll probably only work on some platforms (at
least BeOS, Mac, Unix, and VMS). The reason for its being there is to
spot when the game is being played from some generic games account
rather than an individual one ("games" is also checked; in fact, only
the first four characters are, though case-sensitivity is
platform-dependent), so taking advantage of it is a (useful) hack.

